      "memo_sha256": "7c39d809159f5fd1a886e84b3f3458dabb8bf8dc27dd320e26eac1c5d08104dd",
      "report_home": 4,
      "source_reading": "In the positive-input branch of Theorem 3.1, after correctly asserting that every negative input has loss above loss(0), the proof prints inf_{y <= 0} loss(y) < inf_y loss(y) and later says the unanimous-order loss is lower bounded by loss(0) from above."
    },
